# Michigan Neural Distinctiveness (MiND) Study

This dataset contains multimodal neuroimaging data collected as part of the MiND project,
investigating the scope, causes, and consequences of age-related neural dedifferentiation.

## Modalities
- fMRI: visual categorization, auditory, motor, somatosensory tasks + resting state
- T1-weighted structural MRI
- Diffusion-weighted imaging (DWI/DTI)
- MR Spectroscopy (MEGA-PRESS GABA-edited, 7 cortical ROIs)

## Sessions
- ses-placebo: fMRI + structural + DTI session
- ses-mrs: MRS + structural session (separate day)

## Scanner
GE Discovery MR750 3T, 8-channel head coil
University of Michigan Functional MRI Laboratory


